* Concurrency and parallelism to load and process files in parallel
* Robust error handling and logging mechanisms to track failed attempts and provide detailed reports on file loading failures
* Customizable behavior through environment variables or a configuration file
* Performance optimization for initial loading times and subsequent executions
* Scalability to handle a large number of files efficiently
* Dependency management to ensure that all necessary files are loaded before executing any script
* Resource limits to prevent excessive resource consumption
* Testing and validation suite to validate the functionality of the module under various conditions

The implementation is modular, well-documented, and capable of adapting to changes in file structure or requirements without significant rework."]

