The function returns an instance of `ImageMetadata`, which contains the extracted metadata and the computed hash. The `AdditionalSamples` property is set to an empty string if there are no additional samples in the image, or to a comma-separated list of sample names if there are any.

This code is optimized for performance by using streaming processing to handle large files efficiently without compromising on accuracy. It also takes advantage of the `SixLabors.ImageSharp` library's ability to load and process images in parallel, which can significantly improve performance when handling multiple files concurrently.']

