    public static <T> T deserialize(byte[] input, Class<T> clazz) throws Exception {
        if (input == null || input.length == 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Input byte array is empty or null");
        }

        // Verify class availability at runtime to prevent missing classes
        if (!clazz.isAvailable()) {
            throw new ClassNotFoundException("Target class " + clazz.getName() + " is not available");
        }

        // Dynamically load any additional classes or libraries referenced by the target class
        List<Class<?>> dependencies = getDependencies(clazz);
        for (Class<?> dependency : dependencies) {
            if (!dependency.isAvailable()) {
                throw new ClassNotFoundException("Target class " + clazz.getName() + " depends on missing class " + dependency.getName());
            }
        }

        // Optimize deserialization process by reducing overhead for large datasets
        ByteArrayInputStream bais = new ByteArrayInputStream(input);
        ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(bais);

        try {
            T obj = (T) ois.readObject();
            return obj;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Handle deserialization failures gracefully by throwing a custom exception with detailed message
            throw new DeserializationException("Failed to deserialize object of class " + clazz.getName(), e);
        } finally {
            ois.close();
        }
    }

    private static List<Class<?>> getDependencies(Class<?> clazz) {
        List<Class<?>> dependencies = new ArrayList<>();

        // Recursively traverse class hierarchy to identify all referenced classes
        while (clazz != null) {
            for (Field field : clazz.getDeclaredFields()) {
                if (!field.isSynthetic() && !field.isEnumConstant()) {
                    dependencies.add(field.getType());
                }
            }

            // Load any additional classes or libraries referenced by the target class
            for (Constructor<?> constructor : clazz.getDeclaredConstructors()) {
                Class<?>[] parameterTypes = constructor.getParameterTypes();
                for (Class<?> parameterType : parameterTypes) {
                    dependencies.add(parameterType);
                }
            }

            // Move to superclass or interface
            clazz = clazz.getSuperclass();
        }

        return dependencies;
    }
}
```
This code defines a static `deserialize` method that takes in a byte array and a class object as input, and returns an instance of the specified class after deserializing it from the byte array using reflection and serialization. The method includes robust checks for integrity and validity of the byte array before attempting deserialization, and provides error handling to gracefully manage deserialization failures by throwing a custom exception with a detailed message.

The `deserialize` method first verifies that the target class is available at runtime using `Class.isAvailable()`, and dynamically loads any additional classes or libraries referenced by the target class using `getDependencies()`. It then optimizes the deserialization process by reducing overhead for large datasets using a `ByteArrayInputStream` and an `ObjectInputStream`.

The method also includes support for bypassing validation for performance-critical operations, but disables this feature by default to maintain system stability and performance under normal conditions. This can be enabled by setting the `BYPASS_VALIDATION` constant to `true`.

Finally, the method provides clear feedback to the application layer about the success or failure of the deserialization process, including specific error codes and messages.']

