The class also includes static methods for registering new stream processing functions using `registerStreamProcessor`, and creating new instances of subclasses using `createStreamInstance`. These methods allow developers to add new stream processors and create new instances of the `DataHandler` class with specific data streams, respectively.

To optimize memory usage, the `DataHandler` class uses `Buffer.allocUnsafe` to allocate memory for the buffered data chunks, which avoids unnecessary copying while ensuring minimal memory overhead. Additionally, the class includes a mechanism for handling potential memory allocation failures gracefully, providing fallback strategies if allocations exceed available resources.

