To optimize memory usage, the function implements a resource management policy that releases temporary resources immediately after they are no longer needed during the compilation process. This helps to prevent excessive system resource consumption and performance bottlenecks. The function also considers strategies for parallel processing and load balancing to support high-throughput environments.

Finally, the function ensures that it can handle large-scale projects efficiently by avoiding excessive system resource consumption and performance bottlenecks. It uses a combination of resource management policies and parallel processing techniques to achieve this goal.']

['```php
<?php

function updateClinicStatus($clinicId, $status, $lastModifiedIp, $lastModifiedDate) {
    // Start transaction
    $db->beginTransaction();

    try {
        // Update clinic status
        $stmt = $db->prepare("UPDATE clinics SET status = :status, last_modified_ip = :lastModifiedIp, last_modified_date = :lastModifiedDate WHERE id = :clinicId");
        $stmt->bindParam(':status', $status);
        $stmt->bindParam(':lastModifiedIp', $lastModifiedIp);
        $stmt->bindParam(':lastModifiedDate', $lastModifiedDate);
        $stmt->bindParam(':clinicId', $clinicId);
        $stmt->execute();

        // Commit transaction
        $db->commit();

        return "Successfully updated clinic status";
    } catch (Exception $e) {
        // Rollback transaction
        $db->rollBack();

        throw new Exception("Failed to update clinic status", 0, $e);
    }
}
```
