This implementation is optimized for both single-threaded and multi-threaded execution environments, as it uses a thread pool to process multiple datasets in parallel without excessive memory overhead. It also ensures efficient memory usage by dynamically allocating memory for each dataset and freeing it after processing. Additionally, it includes error handling for invalid inputs and memory allocation failures, which helps prevent crashes or incorrect results.']

