The above code defines a scalable C-based module that manages a dynamic array of `NFAPI_RX_FRAME_INFO_T` structures, each containing a valid `RX_FRAME_TAG`, a `PHY_RRC_CHANNEL_CONFIG_TAG`, and a `PHY_RRC_PHY_FRAME_INFO_TAG`. The module supports efficient addition and updates of new frames, ensuring minimal latency during high-throughput operations. It also implements a caching mechanism to improve performance when dealing with frequently accessed frames.

The memory usage of the module is optimized by using a dynamic array for storing the frames, which allows for efficient resizing of the array as more frames are added. The cache is implemented as a separate data structure that stores recently accessed frames, allowing for fast access to those frames without having to iterate over the entire array.

The overhead introduced by the cache management is minimal, as the cache is only updated when a new frame is added or an existing frame is updated. This ensures that the cache remains up-to-date and does not become stale.

