The client integrates with a third-party logging service for detailed metrics collection, allowing for the monitoring data to be stored and analyzed over time. It also includes a mechanism to periodically validate the integrity of the external data source and implement fallback strategies in case of data discrepancies.

To scale horizontally, the client can be designed to handle increased monitoring demands by adding more instances or adjusting the load balancing strategy. The client can also be designed to support multiple endpoints and API keys for different monitoring services, allowing for a more flexible and scalable architecture.']

