To ensure that no two `flowID`s are the same and all entries are unique, the function uses a nested loop to iterate over each entry in the array and check if any other entry has the same `flowID`. If it finds a duplicate, it generates a new random value for the `flowID` field.

The function then loads initial traffic flow statistics from an external CSV file using `fopen()` and `fgets()`. It parses each line of the CSV file using `sscanf()`, and populates the corresponding entry in the array of `TrafficFlowStats` structures with the parsed values. If any parsing errors are encountered, the function falls back to generating default values using a different random number generator seed.

