To prevent resource exhaustion under heavy load, this code uses a process group to manage the child processes. This allows it to terminate all child processes on SIGINT, which helps to prevent resource exhaustion in case of a user interrupt. It also uses `waitpid()` with the `WNOHANG` option to check for the exit statuses of each command as soon as they are available, rather than waiting for all commands to complete before returning. This helps to ensure that the utility can handle an increasing number of concurrent commands without becoming overwhelmed.']

