Here is an example of how the Java method to establish a connection to a remote address using a Java Channel could be implemented:
```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.InetSocketAddress;
import java.nio.channels.AsynchronousChannelGroup;
import java.nio.channels.AsynchronousServerSocketChannel;
import java.nio.channels.AsynchronousSocketChannel;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
import java.util.concurrent.Executors;

public class ConnectionManager {
    private AsynchronousServerSocketChannel serverSocket;
    private ExecutorService executor;

    public ConnectionManager() throws IOException {
        // Create an asynchronous channel group for the connection manager
        AsynchronousChannelGroup channelGroup = AsynchronousChannelGroup.withFixedThreadPool(1, Executors.defaultThreadFactory());

        // Create a server socket channel and bind it to a local address
        InetSocketAddress localAddress = new InetSocketAddress("localhost", 8080);
        serverSocket = AsynchronousServerSocketChannel.open(channelGroup).bind(localAddress);
    }

    public void start() throws IOException {
        // Start the server socket channel and wait for incoming connections
        executor = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor();
        executor.execute(() -> {
            try {
                serverSocket.accept().get();
            } catch (InterruptedException | ExecutionException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            }
        });
    }

    public void stop() throws IOException {
        // Stop the server socket channel and shut down the executor service
        serverSocket.close();
        executor.shutdownNow();
    }
}
```
This implementation uses an `AsynchronousServerSocketChannel` to listen for incoming connections on a local address, and an `ExecutorService` to handle incoming connections in a separate thread. The `start` method starts the server socket channel and waits for incoming connections, while the `stop` method stops the server socket channel and shuts down the executor service.

