The function also includes error handling for memory allocation failures using `fprintf(stderr, "Error: Failed to allocate memory\n");` and returns if an error occurs.

This implementation is efficient in terms of both time and space complexity as it only allocates memory for the NIC configurations when they are needed, and uses `realloc()` to resize the array of IP addresses associated with each NIC configuration as needed.']

